{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_16-13-10-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && grep -n '\"'^  \"knowledge\"'\"\\\\|\"'^  \"interpretations\"'\"\\\\|\"'^  \"rationale\"'\"\\\\|\"'^  \"investigations\"'\"\\\\|\"'^}'\"' update.json | head && echo \\\"--- tail ---\\\" && tail -6 update.json\"","aggregated_output":"2:  \"rationale\": \"The shutdown experiment completed on a clean copy (CheckRun c5d127c955b549a8888fe6bab568dbce, exit 0) and its single parsed event settles the open question: the accepted duty never completed. On one real cluster the freeze handshake fired (freeze_handshake=inside_restore_read, so the main loop was provably inside the Restore handler and could no longer select on applyCh), the control Barrier on the undisturbed leader returned no error (so the same public call does complete when a producer exists), the leader accepted the Barrier future in state Leader, Shutdown() moved it to state Shutdown, and after the bounded observation the future had still not been responded while queued_in_apply_ch=1 with capacity 64. The release path then returned 'failed to write snapshot: unexpected EOF', confirming that the occupied handler was the node's own main loop and that it resumed and exited cleanly. The recorded discriminator said a completion would defeat the suspicion and must name the responding producer; none occurred, and source shows none can: the logFuture has no ShutdownCh (future.go:113-118 with only the internal restore and snapshot futures wired to shutdownCh), the main loop leaves on shutdownCh and runFSM exits with it, and runLeader's defer responds only futures already on leaderState.inflight. I therefore record the witnessed fact, answer the gap, and assert the scoped defect with its conditions, counterweight and limits stated.\",\n3:  \"knowledge\": [\n25:  \"investigations\": [\n44:  \"interpretations\": [\n80:}\n--- tail ---\n        \"Only the Barrier path was executed. VerifyLeader constructs its verifyFuture without a ShutdownCh too and sends it on a 64-buffered channel (api.go:883-893, api.go:568), so it shares the shape, but that is a source-level observation and was not exercised.\",\n        \"The scenario models a slow caller-supplied stream keeping the handler busy; it does not claim that shutdown always finds a duty in the buffer.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
